    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": " \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 134\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 3261, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  repeal  section  470 of the judiciary law, relating to\n      allowing attorneys having offices in the state  to  reside  in  an\n      adjoining state\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would remove the current requirement that attorneys admitted\nto practice law in New York but who are not residents maintain an actual\nphysical office in the state.\n \n  The  State  has  a responsibility to ensure the adequate oversight and\nregulation of all  attorneys  practicing  in  this  state.  Current  law\nrequires  every attorney practicing in this state to maintain a physical\npresence in the state, whether through residency or through  a  physical\noffice.  It is important to ensure that New Yorkers have adequate access\nto representation, including  by  requiring  offices  to  be  physically\nlocated in New York.\n \n  Therefore, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
    "vetoNumber": 134,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2023
